# Track 5 — Game Adapter Tuning Dimensions — COMPLETE

Date: 2026-09-09
Branch: `build/initial-product`
Application SHA: `8dac70fdb2c693533ae481aaadd846ab84fde228`
Commit: `feat: add capability-honest game adapter tuning dimensions`
Windows CI: #1007 — SUCCESS
Run id: `34416726382`

## Verified scope

- Added optional `IGameTuningDimensionProvider`; `IGameAdapter` remains source-compatible and unchanged.
- Added `GameAdapterTuningDimensionDeclaration` as adapter-owned workload search-space metadata.
- Added pure `UniversalTuningWorkloadDimensionFactory`.
- Workload tuning authority is resolved only through `GameAdapterResolver` from stable `GameIdentity`; PID/path/process/display name never creates tuning authority.
- Generic or unregistered specializations produce zero workload dimensions.
- Adapters without the optional provider produce zero workload dimensions.
- Provider is not invoked unless the resolved adapter proves `ConfigDiscovery + ConfigSnapshot + ConfigMutation + Rollback`.
- Accepted declarations are namespaced as `workload.<normalized-adapter-id>.<normalized-local-id>` with `AuthorityId` from the resolved adapter.
- Candidate values preserve exact provider text/order.
- Blank/empty/null/duplicate declarations fail closed.
- Returned dimensions are deterministically ordered.
- Existing `UniversalTuningSearchSpacePlanner` composes System + Workload dimensions; no second compositor or hidden game axis was added.
- Generic and current BlueStacks/FF adapters do not receive invented static dimensions in this slice.
- Existing BlueStacks/FF specialized `TuningCandidate` / `AutoTunerEngine` / runtime/session path remains unchanged.
- Search-space support is exploration only and grants no evidence, recommendation, winner, persistence or mutation authority.

